From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:45:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): preserve quota startup result across owner loss
 echo [daveey]

Why: a managed worker refused startup with SubscriptionQuotaUnavailable (75),
then the owner's worker_lost replaced its attributed result with exit None.
The submitter saw unknown and appended exit 1; mixed modern/unmarked evidence
held the claim until Board expiry charged stale_lease toward triage.

Keep an already attributable non-continuable failed interpreter result. The
owner loss stays diagnostic rather than erasing quota reset/provider evidence.
Keep clean, malformed, continuable, owner-restart and rebound evidence on their
existing witnessed-loss path. Existing exact-run/process death fences still
control closure; this is not permission to reclaim a live interpreter.

Proof: main a0e7a51c06679aaf38d9303925e796d202912ad4 RED: new regression
left the claim running. Final suite RED on unchanged production: 2 failed,
5 passed. GREEN: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_quota_start_loss.py (7),
test_kanban_rebound_worker_loss.py (8), test_kanban_owner_restart_failed_receipt.py
(31), test_kanban_owner_death.py (13), plus causal/receipt consumer suites.
Native subprocess writes typed quota receipt, owner records loss, submitter
processes unknown; next dispatcher tick releases claim, preserves failures=1
with limit2 and holds until >= reset. Four guard mutants (type, zero,
continuable, owner role) each fail the corresponding negative control.
scripts/check --base origin/main: 20 checks OK.

Scope boundary: authoritative Board alarm-first recovery is separately owned
by t_01a1d81f668a5221; this core PR prevents the startup cause from being lost,
not a claim that the Board server's expiry behavior has shipped. Parent
 t_01a1d817931fa926 remains open for both scopes and deployment verification.
No live prevention observation yet.
